{
  "raw": {
    "https://clarku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205066": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Clark University\nJob Posting: Associate Director of Admissions Clark University \n\tJob Posting: Associate Director of Admissions Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Director of Admissions Category: Staff and Administrators Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: UADM-UG Admissions Office 2210 Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Sep 22, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time - Exempt Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $51,700.00 - $68,150.00 Position ID: 205066 Share About Clark University: Founded in 1887, Clark was one of the first all-graduate institutions in the United States. Today the University is a highly-ranked, student-centered institution educating approximately 2,100 undergraduate and 1,150 graduate students to be imaginative and contributing citizens of the world and to advance the frontiers of knowledge and understanding through rigorous scholarship and creative effort. This commitment to scholarship and inquiry reflects the University's commitment to \"challenge convention and change our world\" and to address issues of critical importance to society. It is also reflected by Clark's many national and international distinctions, including innovation, community engagement and impact, as a top green campus, and for having a distinguished geography and international development program. Clark has also been included in the groundbreaking Colleges that Change Lives guide since it was first published in 1996. Clark is located in Worcester, Massachusetts, a dynamic, diverse city \"on the rise\". The second largest city in New England, Worcester is home to 10 institutions of higher learning and is increasingly recognized for its growing healthcare and biotechnology communities, its thriving cultural scene, and as a vibrant food hub. Job Description: Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Undergraduate Admissions, the Associate Director of Undergraduate Admission plays a key role in the execution of Clark University's undergraduate recruitment and enrollment strategy. The Associate Director is responsible for managing an assigned recruitment territory, evaluating applications, representing the University at recruitment events, supervising admissions staff, and developing innovative outreach initiatives that support institutional enrollment goals. The Associate Director serves as a visible representative of Clark University both on and off campus and collaborates closely with admission colleagues, campus partners, alumni, counselors, and families to promote the University's distinctive educational experience. The successful candidate will bring strong relationship-building skills, strategic thinking, data-informed decision making, and a commitment to providing an exceptional experience for prospective students and families. Primary Responsibilities Travel and Recruitment Conduct 6 to 8 weeks of recruitment travel throughout the year Manage recruitment efforts within assigned territories to support institutional enrollment objectives Coordinate all aspects of territory management, including travel planning, school visits, college fairs, alumni events, and other recruitment activities Build and maintain strong relationships with prospective students, families, school counselors, community-based organizations, and other external partners Conduct admissions interviews and represent Clark University through presentations, information sessions, and recruitment programming First-Year Application Review Review and evaluate undergraduate applications in accordance with admissions policies, enrollment priorities, and holistic review practices Make recommendations regarding admissions decisions and participate actively in committee discussions Campus Visitor Experience and Counselor of the Day Responsibilities Serve as a resource for prospective students and families visiting campus Conduct information sessions, admissions interviews, and other visitor engagement programs designed to communicate the value of a Clark education Perform Counselor of the Day responsibilities, including responding to inquiries, addressing visitor concerns, and providing admissions guidance Partner with campus stakeholders to ensure a welcoming, informative, and student-centered campus visit experience Leadership, Staff Supervision, and Special Projects Supervise, mentor, and develop assigned admissions staff to support individual growth and departmental success Serve as a resource and leader within the Undergraduate Admissions team, providing guidance on recruitment strategy, territory management, and student engagement initiatives Oversee day-to-day operations of one or more functional areas within Undergraduate Admissions, such as family engagement, counselor relations, or special enrollment initiatives Participate in departmental committees, cross-functional projects, and university initiatives Foster a collaborative, inclusive, and student-centered team culture Administrative Support Maintain accurate records and data within the University's CRM system and related enrollment management platforms Prepare reports, analyze recruitment and enrollment trends, and contribute to data-informed decision making Perform other duties and special projects as assigned in support of Undergraduate Admissions and University Enrollment goals Requirements: Qualifications and Experience Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree preferred Minimum 4-6 years of progressive experience in undergraduate admissions, enrollment management, college counseling, or a related field Experience supervising, mentoring, or developing professional staff, student employees, or graduate assistants preferred Demonstrated success in student recruitment, territory management, application review, and enrollment-focused initiatives Valid driver's license and willingness to travel extensively throughout the recruitment cycle Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong relationship-building, judgment, and interpersonal skills Strong analytical skills and ability to utilize data to inform recruitment strategies and decision-making Excellent written, verbal, presentation, and public speaking skills Ability to manage multiple priorities, work independently, and contribute effectively in a fast-paced environment Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Commitment to ethical practices and compliance with all relevant policies and regulations Familiarity with admissions CRM platforms (preferably Slate) and enrollment management technologies Demonstrated commitment to student-centered service, access, and inclusive excellence Ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues, families, school counselors, and campus stakeholders Experience leading projects, initiatives, or functional areas within an admissions or enrollment organization Ability to supervise, mentor, and develop staff while fostering a collaborative and high-performing team environment Additional Information: Expected Hiring Range: $51,700 to $68,150 Pay Transparency Disclosure: The compensation for this position will be determined based on factors that include available budget, internal equity, and the selected candidate's qualifications, experience, education, and other job-related credentials. This range represents Clark University's good-faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting consistent with Clark's compensation philosophy and internal alignment. At Clark University we believe that diversity of experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds leads to a more innovative and productive work environment. We welcome and encourage individuals of all backgrounds to join our team and contribute their unique ideas to help us achieve our goals. Clark University offers a generous benefit package for full and, if applicable, part-time employees that include; paid time off, generous retirement plan, group health and dental insurance, life insurance, and tuition, along with use of many campus amenities. For a complete list of benefits for eligible employees visit here . To review the Clark University Police Department Annual Security and Fire Safety Report visit here . Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must submit your credentials online. Create a Clark University Careers Account by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. You will be able to upload the following documents, which are required for consideration: Resume Cover letter See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Already have a Clark University Careers Account? Login to your account to add documents or update your account. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary will be commensurate with skills and experience. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States for any employer. Clark University participates in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the United States. A successful background check is required upon acceptance. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Clark University 950 Main Street Worcester, MA 01610"
    },
    "https://clarku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205120": {
      "title": "Central Utility Plant Operator",
      "description": "Clark University\nJob Posting: Central Utility Plant Operator Clark University \n\tJob Posting: Central Utility Plant Operator Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Central Utility Plant Operator Category: Staff and Administrators Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: FM-Power Plant 6210 Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Sep 23, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time - Non Exempt Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $27.65 - $36.35 Position ID: 205120 Share About Clark University: Founded in 1887, Clark was one of the first all-graduate institutions in the United States. Today the University is a highly-ranked, student-centered institution educating approximately 2,350 undergraduate and 1,150 graduate students to be imaginative and contributing citizens of the world and to advance the frontiers of knowledge and understanding through rigorous scholarship and creative effort. This commitment to scholarship and inquiry reflects the University's commitment to \"challenge convention and change our world\" and to address issues of critical importance to society. It is also reflected by Clark's many national and international distinctions, including innovation, community engagement and impact, as a top green campus, and for having a distinguished geography and international development program. Clark has also been included in the groundbreaking Colleges that Change Lives guide since it was first published in 1996. Clark is located in Worcester, Massachusetts, a dynamic, diverse city \"on the rise\". The second largest city in New England, Worcester is home to 11 institutions of higher learning and is increasingly recognized for its growing healthcare and biotechnology communities, its thriving cultural scene, and as a vibrant food hub. Job Description: Basic Function Reporting to the Chief Engineer, the Plant Operator operates and maintains the Central Utility Plant in accordance with Massachusetts General Law Chapter 146, Section 49. The Operator monitors and maintains steam, hot water, cooling, and cogeneration systems in the Central Utility Plant (CUP), including all other auxiliary components, on a day-to-day basis. Major Responsibilities Equipment Monitoring Operate and maintain the CUP during an assigned shift. This includes monitoring water levels and steam or water pressure, and maintaining records, logs, charts, and reports related to plant operations. Place boilers online or offline according to demand. Perform routine maintenance in the boiler room and cogeneration plant areas. Perform boiler water treatment tests during the shift. Manually add chemicals and water to chemical tanks. Maintain adequate fuel levels and add fuel when needed. Record hourly readings for boilers, the natural gas reciprocating engine, and generator equipment. Equipment Preventive Maintenance Follow all maintenance schedules for CUP equipment. Clean, paint, and lubricate CUP auxiliary equipment as needed. Sweep, mop, and paint floors within the CUP as directed by the Chief Engineer. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements: Requirements High school or vocational school diploma and at least five years of experience operating and maintaining cogeneration plant systems, high-pressure boilers, and related Central Utility Plant equipment, or an equivalent combination of training and experience. Must possess a Massachusetts 2A/1C Hoisting License or obtain one within one year. Must possess a Massachusetts Second Class Fireman's License or higher. Must have in-depth knowledge of troubleshooting high-pressure boilers and cogeneration equipment, and the ability to apply safe work practices around high-pressure boilers and high-speed rotating equipment. Must be able to lift 50 pounds; bend, stoop, and twist daily; stand, walk, or sit for extended periods; climb stairs and ladders; and open and close valves atop boilers. Preferred qualifications include basic pipefitting and welding skills and proficiency with Word, Excel, a computerized maintenance management system (CMMS), Outlook email, and common web-based applications. This position is considered essential personnel. The employee must be available for 24-hour emergency call and periodic emergency shift coverage due to other operators' absences. The employee is expected to report to work during emergency closings and may occasionally work evenings, weekends, or holidays to respond to University events, facility incidents, or urgent needs. Must maintain positive, professional relationships with members of the Clark community. This job description does not contain a comprehensive list of the activities, duties, or responsibilities required for this position. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. Additional Information: Expected Hiring Range: $27.65 to $36.35 pre hour Pay Transparency Disclosure: The compensation for this position will be determined based on factors that include available budget, internal equity, and the selected candidate's qualifications, experience, education, and other job-related credentials. This range represents Clark University's good-faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting consistent with Clark's compensation philosophy and internal alignment. At Clark University we believe that diversity of experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds leads to a more innovative and productive work environment. We welcome and encourage individuals of all backgrounds to join our team and contribute their unique ideas to help us achieve our goals. Clark University offers a generous benefit package for full and, if applicable, part-time employees that include; paid time off, generous retirement plan, group health and dental insurance, life insurance, and tuition, along with use of many campus amenities. For a complete list of benefits for eligible employees visit here . To review the Clark University Police Department Annual Security and Fire Safety Report visit here . Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must submit your credentials online. Create a Clark University Careers Account by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. You will be able to upload the following documents, which are required for consideration: Resume Cover letter See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Already have a Clark University Careers Account? Login to your account to add documents or update your account. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary will be commensurate with skills and experience. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States for any employer. Clark University participates in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the United States. A successful background check is required upon acceptance. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Clark University 950 Main Street Worcester, MA 01610"
