    "https://clarku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204887": {
      "title": "Clinical Coordinator and Assistant / Associate Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Clark University\nJob Posting: Clinical Coordinator and Assistant / Associate Professor of Practice Clark University \n\tJob Posting: Clinical Coordinator and Assistant / Associate Professor of Practice Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Clinical Coordinator and Assistant / Associate Professor of Practice Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: PSYC-Psychology 4481 Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Sep 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time - Exempt Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $59,700.00 - $75,600.00 Position ID: 204887 Share About Clark University: Founded in 1887, Clark was one of the first all-graduate institutions in the United States. Today the University is a highly-ranked, student-centered institution educating approximately 2,350 undergraduate and 1,150 graduate students to be imaginative and contributing citizens of the world and to advance the frontiers of knowledge and understanding through rigorous scholarship and creative effort. This commitment to scholarship and inquiry reflects the University's commitment to \"challenge convention and change our world\" and to address issues of critical importance to society. It is also reflected by Clark's many national and international distinctions, including innovation, community engagement and impact, as a top green campus, and for having a distinguished geography and international development program. Clark has also been included in the groundbreaking Colleges that Change Lives guide since it was first published in 1996. Clark is located in Worcester, Massachusetts, a dynamic, diverse city \"on the rise\". The second largest city in New England, Worcester is home to 11 institutions of higher learning and is increasingly recognized for its growing healthcare and biotechnology communities, its thriving cultural scene, and as a vibrant food hub. Job Description: The Department of Psychology invites applications for the position of Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice and Clinical Training Coordinator to begin in January 2027. This is a full-time, non-tenure-track position with a renewable multi-year contract. This new hire will work with the new Director to continue the launch of a newly established Master of Arts in Mental Health Counseling program. Noted for its rich history in Psychology, Clark University offers the advantages of both a distinguished research university and a small liberal arts college (see https://www.clarku.edu/departments/psychology/). The Psychology Department has Ph.D. programs in Social, Clinical, and Developmental Psychology and a popular undergraduate major. We seek candidates with an M.A., Ph.D. or Psy.D. in Mental Health Counseling, Clinical or Counseling Psychology, Counseling Education, or related discipline who will play a central role in coordinating and overseeing students' clinical training experiences for a new M.A. program in Mental Health Counseling within the Department. Clinical Coordinator and Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice must be licensed or license-eligible as a mental health counselor in Massachusetts, with a minimum of three years' experience post-licensure. The ideal candidate will coordinate all aspects of clinical training in the M.A. Program, including practicum and externship placements, recruit, maintain, and develop partnerships with community agencies, hospitals, schools, counseling centers, and other possible training sites, and supervise and support students during in-house clinical practica, ensuring quality, compliance, consistent training standards, and professional growth. The successful candidate will bring substantial experience in professional counseling practice, a strong record of clinical supervision or training, establishing or managing field placement or community partnership programs, and a commitment to preparing the next generation of mental health professionals within a social justice-oriented, community-engaged academic environment. The primary responsibilities will include: Coordinate clinical training of M.A. students in the program, including establishing and maintaining partnerships with clinical training sites Teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in counseling theories, group counseling, clinical interventions, or career counseling Collaborate with university administrators, faculty, and staff to ensure program quality, accreditation readiness, and adherence to best practices in mental health counseling training Maintain engagement in clinical practice Participate actively in departmental and university service Requirements: General: M.A., Ph.D. or Psy.D. in Mental Health Counseling, Clinical or Counseling Psychology, Counseling Education, or related discipline Licensed or license-eligible as a mental health counselor in Massachusetts At least three (3) years' experience post licensure Ability to support inclusive learning and practice environments. Capacity and willingness for leadership Regarding teaching and mentoring: Ability to teach basic and specialized topics in mental health counseling Ability to provide clinical supervision Demonstrated ability and interest to mentor graduate students Experience and/or careful consideration of how to work with students from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred: General: Track record of mental health counseling and supervision experience Regarding administrative skills: Track record in curriculum development and program accreditation Track record of managing field placement or community partnerships Regarding teaching and mentoring: Ability to teach basic and specialized topics in mental health counseling, counseling theories, career counseling, clinical interventions, and group counseling Demonstrated ability and interest to mentor undergraduate students. Regarding connection with department and university as a whole: Synergy with existing interests in the program, department, and university Additional Information: Expected Hiring Range: $59,700 to $75,600 Pay Transparency Disclosure: The compensation for this position will be determined based on factors that include available budget, internal equity, and the selected candidate's qualifications, experience, education, and other job-related credentials. This range represents Clark University's good-faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting consistent with Clark's compensation philosophy and internal alignment. At Clark University we believe that diversity of experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds leads to a more innovative and productive work environment. We welcome and encourage individuals of all backgrounds to join our team and contribute their unique ideas to help us achieve our goals. Clark University offers a generous benefit package for full and, if applicable, part-time employees that include; paid time off, generous retirement plan, group health and dental insurance, life insurance, and tuition, along with use of many campus amenities. For a complete list of benefits for eligible employees visit here . To review the Clark University Police Department Annual Security and Fire Safety Report visit here . Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must submit your credentials online. Create a Clark University Careers Account by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. You will be able to upload the following documents, which are required for consideration: Resume Cover letter See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Already have a Clark University Careers Account? Login to your account to add documents or update your account. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary will be commensurate with skills and experience. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States for any employer. Clark University participates in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the United States. A successful background check is required upon acceptance. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Clark University 950 Main Street Worcester, MA 01610"
