    "https://clarku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205615": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student Employment",
      "description": "Clark University\nJob Posting: Assistant Director, Student Employment Clark University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director, Student Employment Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director, Student Employment Category: Staff and Administrators Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: OSE - Student Employment 3113 Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Oct 7, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time - Exempt Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $44,800.00 - $60,250.00 Position ID: 205615 Share About Clark University: Founded in 1887, Clark was one of the first all-graduate institutions in the United States. Today the University is a highly-ranked, student-centered institution educating approximately 2,350 undergraduate and 1,150 graduate students to be imaginative and contributing citizens of the world and to advance the frontiers of knowledge and understanding through rigorous scholarship and creative effort. This commitment to scholarship and inquiry reflects the University's commitment to \"challenge convention and change our world\" and to address issues of critical importance to society. It is also reflected by Clark's many national and international distinctions, including innovation, community engagement and impact, as a top green campus, and for having a distinguished geography and international development program. Clark has also been included in the groundbreaking Colleges that Change Lives guide since it was first published in 1996. Clark is located in Worcester, Massachusetts, a dynamic, diverse city \"on the rise\". The second largest city in New England, Worcester is home to 11 institutions of higher learning and is increasingly recognized for its growing healthcare and biotechnology communities, its thriving cultural scene, and as a vibrant food hub. Job Description: Reporting to the Director of Student Employment, the Assistant Director provides operational and strategic support for Clark University's campus-wide student employment program. The position ensures that students, faculty, and staff have an accessible, efficient, and well-supported student employment experience while maintaining effective systems, processes, and practices that are compliant with federal and state law.  Student employment is an important component of the Clark experience, providing students with opportunities to earn income, build relationships, develop professional competencies, apply learning, and contribute to the University community. The Assistant Director provides the infrastructure necessary to support these experiences at scale. The position works closely with Human Resources, Payroll, Financial Assistance, the International Center, Career Development, academic and administrative departments, and student employment supervisors. The Assistant Director serves as a key campus resource for student employment policies, processes, systems, and problem resolution. Student Employment Operations, Payroll & Compliance Lead the day-to-day operational processes associated with student employment onboarding for undergraduate and graduate students, ensuring timely, accurate, and accessible processes for students and supervisors. Review and process student employment documentation, including job records, I-9 and identity verification processes, and other required employment documentation in accordance with University procedures and applicable requirements. Serve as a primary resource for students, faculty, and staff regarding student employment policies, procedures, requirements, and problem resolution. Coordinate with Payroll and Human Resources throughout the biweekly student employment payroll process, including review, correction, reconciliation, and final sign-off. Supervise and support student employees engaged in student employment operations, communications, and data-related work. Systems, Data & Process Management Serve as a primary administrator and campus resource for student employment systems, including Banner, Handshake, and related HR/employment technology. Work collaboratively with Financial Assistance, the International Center, Human Resources, Payroll, and campus departments to resolve student employment issues and ensure timely follow-through. Assist with budget management, purchasing, and other administrative functions related to the program. Student Employment Experience & Engagement Oversee communications and outreach related to student employment, including digital communications, marketing, and annual student employment initiatives. Support programming and recognition efforts, including National Student Employment Week. Collaborate with Student Success and campus partners to develop programs, resources, and communications that help students understand and maximize the developmental and career value of student employment. Student Success, Community Engagement, and Inclusion Center equity, inclusion and student voice while critically working to ensure student engagement, belonging, wellbeing, retention, and success. Play a key role in campus traditions and high-level university initiatives and experiences, such as opening weekend, undergraduate onboarding, orientation, commencement, family weekend, traditional events, etc. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required. Demonstrated experience managing complex administrative processes, preferably in higher education, human resources, student employment, student services, or a related field. Strong organizational skills and exceptional attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain accurate records in a high-volume environment. Demonstrated ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, and requirements, exercise sound judgment, and resolve complex or sensitive issues appropriately. Strong technology and systems skills, including the ability to learn, administer, and troubleshoot database, employment, and student information systems. Demonstrated ability to identify opportunities for process improvement, develop effective procedures, and implement solutions that improve efficiency, accuracy, accessibility, and the user experience. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build effective working relationships and provide responsive, respectful service to students, faculty, staff, supervisors, and campus partners with diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively across organizational units and coordinate work involving multiple stakeholders, systems, and processes. Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion and sound judgment. Commitment to creating accessible, equitable, and student-centered processes and experiences. Preferred Qualifications Experience with student employment, human resources, payroll, financial aid, career development, or related higher education functions. Experience using data to monitor processes, identify trends, and inform program or operational improvements. Experience developing training, resources, or communications for diverse campus audiences. Experience supporting student employment as an experiential learning or career-development opportunity. Additional Information: Working Conditions and Physical Requirements Primarily on-site with occasional evening and weekend responsibilities. Expected Hiring Range: $44,800 to $60,250 Pay Transparency Disclosure: The compensation for this position will be determined based on factors that include available budget, internal equity, and the selected candidate's qualifications, experience, education, and other job-related credentials. This range represents Clark University's good-faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting consistent with Clark's compensation philosophy and internal alignment. At Clark University we believe that diversity of experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds leads to a more innovative and productive work environment. We welcome and encourage individuals of all backgrounds to join our team and contribute their unique ideas to help us achieve our goals. Clark University offers a generous benefit package for full and, if applicable, part-time employees that include; paid time off, generous retirement plan, group health and dental insurance, life insurance, and tuition, along with use of many campus amenities. For a complete list of benefits for eligible employees visit here . To review the Clark University Police Department Annual Security and Fire Safety Report visit here . Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must submit your credentials online. Create a Clark University Careers Account by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. You will be able to upload the following documents, which are required for consideration: Resume Cover letter See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Already have a Clark University Careers Account? Login to your account to add documents or update your account. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary will be commensurate with skills and experience. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States for any employer. Clark University participates in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the United States. A successful background check is required upon acceptance. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Clark University 950 Main Street Worcester, MA 01610"
    },
    "https://clarku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204373": {
      "title": "Community Director",
      "description": "Clark University\nJob Posting: Community Director Clark University \n\tJob Posting: Community Director Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Community Director Category: Staff and Administrators Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: RLH Housing - Administration 3221 Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Sep 2, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time - Exempt Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $44,800.00 - $60,250.00 Position ID: 204373 Share About Clark University: Founded in 1887, Clark was one of the first all-graduate institutions in the United States. Today the University is a highly-ranked, student-centered institution educating approximately 2,350 undergraduate and 1,150 graduate students to be imaginative and contributing citizens of the world and to advance the frontiers of knowledge and understanding through rigorous scholarship and creative effort. This commitment to scholarship and inquiry reflects the University's commitment to \"challenge convention and change our world\" and to address issues of critical importance to society. It is also reflected by Clark's many national and international distinctions, including innovation, community engagement and impact, as a top green campus, and for having a distinguished geography and international development program. Clark has also been included in the groundbreaking Colleges that Change Lives guide since it was first published in 1996. Clark is located in Worcester, Massachusetts, a dynamic, diverse city \"on the rise\". The second largest city in New England, Worcester is home to 11 institutions of higher learning and is increasingly recognized for its growing healthcare and biotechnology communities, its thriving cultural scene, and as a vibrant food hub. Job Description: The Community Director is a full-time, 11-month, live-in professional staff member responsible for leading a residential community of up to 600 first-year and/or upper-class students at Clark University. This position works a minimum of 40 hours per week and requires regular evening and weekend commitments, including participation in a rotating on-call schedule to support after-hours crisis response and student safety. The Community Director plays a key role in fostering a student-centered, inclusive, and educational residential experience aligned with the mission of Residential Life & Housing and the Division of Student Success. The position supervises 8-15 Resident Advisers and provides leadership in residential education, student support, conduct administration, housing operations, and community engagement. The Community Director collaborates closely with campus partners to promote student success, retention, and holistic development. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Residential Education & Community Development (35%) Leads the development and implementation of a comprehensive Residential Curriculum within the assigned community. Supervises, trains, and evaluates 8-15 Resident Advisers through regular one-on-one meetings, weekly staff meetings, and ongoing coaching. Oversees departmental committees, including leadership development, programming plans, and budget management. Ensures the delivery and assessment of educational, social, and community-building initiatives that promote belonging, engagement, and student development. Maintains high visibility within the residential community and collaborates with faculty and campus partners to enhance the student experience. Student Support, Conduct, & Crisis Management (25%) Serves as a University Hearing Officer, adjudicating student conduct cases in accordance with institutional policies. Participates in the professional on-call rotation, responding to emergencies, policy violations, and crisis situations. Serves as a case manager within the Care Team, attending weekly meetings and coordinating support plans for students experiencing academic, personal, or housing-related challenges. Provides referrals, follow-up, and documentation to ensure holistic student support and community safety. Housing Operations & Administrative Management (20%) Supports the operational management of assigned residential facilities in collaboration with the Assistant Director for Housing Operations or designee. Coordinates hall openings and closings. Manages occupancy processes, including room assignments, room changes, room condition reports, health and safety inspections, and damage billing. Submits and tracks maintenance requests in partnership with Facilities. Manages programming and staff development budgets. Maintains accurate records and contributes to departmental assessment and reporting efforts. Departmental Leadership & Divisional Engagement (15%) Contributes to departmental initiatives including RA recruitment, selection, training, and ongoing assessment efforts. Serves on committees and participates in divisional and university-wide programs such as Orientation, Opening Weekend, Family Weekend, and Commencement. Collaborates with campus partners to support student retention and success. Promotes diversity, equity, inclusion, and student voice within residential communities. Communicates regularly with supervisors regarding community trends, risks, and strategic priorities. Performs other duties as assigned in support of departmental and divisional goals. Requirements: Required Qualifications Master's degree in Higher Education Administration, Student Development, Student Personnel or related field Flexible and adaptable, high-energy approach to student development and proven ability to engage students. Strong understanding of student development. Commitment to equity, inclusion, and fostering a residential environment that supports a diverse student body. Ability and willingness to live on campus and serve in an on-call rotation for student emergencies. Preferred Qualifications Previous residential life experience at the RA or professional level. Knowledge of facilities operations or coordination in a residential campus environment. Working Conditions and Physical Requirements Office-based Live-on required Lifting up to 25lbs Additional Information: Expected Hiring Range: $44,800 to $60,250 Pay Transparency Disclosure: The compensation for this position will be determined based on factors that include available budget, internal equity, and the selected candidate's qualifications, experience, education, and other job-related credentials. This range represents Clark University's good-faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting consistent with Clark's compensation philosophy and internal alignment. At Clark University we believe that diversity of experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds leads to a more innovative and productive work environment. We welcome and encourage individuals of all backgrounds to join our team and contribute their unique ideas to help us achieve our goals. Clark University offers a generous benefit package for full and, if applicable, part-time employees that include; paid time off, generous retirement plan, group health and dental insurance, life insurance, and tuition, along with use of many campus amenities. For a complete list of benefits for eligible employees visit here . To review the Clark University Police Department Annual Security and Fire Safety Report visit here . Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must submit your credentials online. Create a Clark University Careers Account by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. You will be able to upload the following documents, which are required for consideration: Resume Cover letter See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Already have a Clark University Careers Account? Login to your account to add documents or update your account. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary will be commensurate with skills and experience. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States for any employer. Clark University participates in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the United States. A successful background check is required upon acceptance. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Clark University 950 Main Street Worcester, MA 01610"
